    "title": "If You've Got Nothing to Hide",
    "text": "• The phrase 'If you've got nothing to hide' is often used in discussions about privacy and surveillance.\n• It suggests that individuals should not be concerned about privacy if they are not engaging in illegal activities.\n• Critics argue that this mindset undermines the importance of personal privacy and civil liberties.\n• The debate over privacy versus security has intensified with advancements in technology and data collection.\n• Various studies indicate that a significant portion of the population values privacy, regardless of their activities.",
